{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory handled cytopenia danger well: the doctor repeatedly screened fever/bleeding/respiratory or neurologic decline, escalated falling counts back to the original hematology service, clarified medication uncertainty, and obtained family receipt of the urgent-return plan. However, the family explicitly raised privacy-sensitive non-cooperation/mental-state concerns, and the doctor never explored psychiatric/adherence barriers or gave a privacy-preserving disclosure plan to the oncology team; this is a minor responsibility-chain omission under RC4. Because any minor in-chain error caps the grade at 2, the completed follow-up repair work cannot raise the trajectory above borderline.",
